                    <death when="1838"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Brother of Charles Maurice de Talleyrand, French foreign minister and prince, who switched
    allegiances from Napoleon to the Bourbons.</p>
                        <p> 'Perigord jr', who Godwin meets at the same meal he meets Archambeau de Talleyrand Perigord
  (25.12.1795) is likely to be Archambeau de Talleyrand Perigord's son <persName key="PER08">Edmond de 
  Talleyrand-Périgord (1787-1872</persName>), who became a general in the Napoleonic wars. </p>
                        <p>Perigord is correctly entered in the 1796 lists under 1795.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Philip G. Dwyer, <title>Talleyrand</title> (London: Longman, 2002)</bibl>
